        "t1": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p><strong>Newport Beach projects: harbor, bluffs and rooftops</strong></p><p>Newport Beach is built around its harbor. Balboa Island, Lido Isle, Linda Isle and the bay side of the Balboa Peninsula have homes with decks a few feet above the water. There the deck railing is the only thing between the living room and the boats. On the ocean side of the Peninsula, three-story homes end in a rooftop deck that needs a 42\" guard around its edge. Corona del Mar and Newport Coast sit on bluffs above the beach and Crystal Cove, where terraces face south and west.</p><p>A frameless glass railing, each panel held by two spigots with no posts, suits all three settings. We ship 48\" deck and rooftop railings, and 60\" pool enclosures for Newport Coast and Big Canyon backyards. Interior remodels in Dover Shores and Newport Heights order custom stair glass.</p>"
          }
        },
        "t2": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p><strong>Salt air every day: why the hardware matters here</strong></p><p>Salt air is constant in Newport Beach, not just on windy days, and it is hard on plated and painted steel. Our spigots, connectors, hinges, latches and caprail are 2205 marine-grade stainless steel with a 10-year no-rust promise, in Brushed Stainless or Matte Black. The 12 mm tempered panels carry a lifetime warranty against manufacturing defects. A fresh-water rinse when you wash the windows keeps the salt film off.</p><p>The California code sets 42\" as the minimum guard height even for a house, and 60\" for a pool enclosure. The City of Newport Beach Community Development Department applies the 2022 Title 24 codes. Much of the city lies in the coastal zone, so ask them what review your address needs. The <a href=\"/pages/california-building-standards-code-for-glass-railings\">California code page</a> has the full summary.</p>"
          }
        },
        "t3": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p><strong>Delivery to Newport Beach and installing it yourself</strong></p><p>Orders are processed in 2–3 business days, then delivered in 5–10 business days by freight carrier with liftgate delivery. On Balboa Island and the Peninsula the streets and alleys are narrow. Tell us how a truck can reach you when you order; the driver lowers the crate at the curb. The price at checkout is final, with no duties, tariffs or hidden fees, and orders over 3,000 USD ship free. Report any damage within 3 days of delivery and before installation for a free replacement or refund.</p><p>The system is designed for DIY installation. Most standard installations take about 4 hours with the <a href=\"/pages/glass-railing-installation-guide\">installation guide</a> and videos. Top-mount spigots bolt to a concrete slab or wood deck; side-mount spigots bolt to the fascia and keep a narrow bayfront deck clear. Engineering documents cover both.</p>"
          }
        }
